WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.669
Stage one: the start line.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.619
To get going, three lines: a git clone, a cd, then install dot sh.

3
00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:16.260
On macOS or Linux, with bash, curl and git. The script does the rest.

4
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:23.077
It installs uv, then garmin-mcp, limited to an allow-list of tools.

5
00:00:23.177 --> 00:00:32.622
It sets up your IDE: Claude Code, Copilot, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, Cursor or Windsurf. Plus your working folders.

6
00:00:33.472 --> 00:00:38.671
Choose your staff: coach and nutritionist only, or everyone but the doctor.

7
00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:45.997
No Garmin watch? Use Intervals dot I C U. The workspace option keeps your data in a private repo.

8
00:00:46.847 --> 00:00:50.745
One Garmin Connect sign-in, two-factor code included.

9
00:00:50.845 --> 00:00:56.684
The tokens stay in your home folder, valid for about six months. Never in the project.

10
00:00:57.534 --> 00:01:04.205
In your IDE, /coach-setup runs a short interview: staff, discipline, coaching style.

11
00:01:04.305 --> 00:01:08.523
Garmin pre-fills your profile, and you confirm each value.

12
00:01:08.623 --> 00:01:12.116
The result: an athlete profile and a goal sheet.

13
00:01:12.966 --> 00:01:21.664
In doubt? /coach-doctor checks the install without writing anything: tokens, Garmin server, config, profile, index.

14
00:01:21.764 --> 00:01:23.102
All green.

15
00:01:23.952 --> 00:01:26.421
First question: /today.

16
00:01:26.521 --> 00:01:31.400
Today's session, the morning check, and the weather window. In three lines.

17
00:01:34.652 --> 00:01:37.398
To go further: the quick start guide.
